Z||000000||contra||09-21-2000||10:55 PM||||I'm just trying to gather information for the future of my fiero. Cost wise, i am looking at a carb. v8 fiero, what kind of engines could i use? and how much simpler is it to install a carb'd v8 into a fiero than a fuel injected one? I know it's not simple at all, but what changes would need to be made etc. I'm asking because somebody who's buying fiero parts off me told me of how they swapped one into their fiero, running around 400+HP and it was relatively easy with the kit they got for around $1500. The engine cost them around $1500, and it took a few weeks to drop in. can anybody post more info? thanx alot<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-22-2000||10:15 AM||||if you have an automatic read the TH125 article in my cave. There is a tranny issue caused by disabling the ECM. It kills the torque Converter locking. I'm working on a fix for it for someone else already. (there is even a prototype TC lockup control in the works. It's manually activated with auto release.)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||contra||09-22-2000||10:35 AM||||yeah i sort of figured something like the tranny would need to be modd'd<BR>if i were converting to a V8 however, i probably would use the 4speed tranny and clutch system i have sitting in my backyard from an 86SE<BR>sure i would love to have a 5speed, but i might as well use what i have.<BR>i'm not planning to do this conversion any time soon at all, i am just considering it, and looking at the facts, and cost. There's alot of friendly people here in toronto who could assist me if i ever did go through the swap though, so that's reassuring<BR>thanx<BR>||||reg||1
