Z||000008||Philphine||09-23-2000||06:30 PM||||fotofrank asked my question. we have vet testing in louisville and while i think i might get some kind of break if i do an '84 (i think around '84-5 is when the testing gets a little more lenient for newer cars), i'd be doing an '87.<P>i did just read on the vette forum thatit would probaly be easy to pass with a 305, especially fuel injected.<P>just went to an outdoor auto show and cruise. listening to those v8's makes it hard to settle for less.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||09-25-2000||09:41 AM||||Emision tests go by year of the car to a point. It depends on what state you are in.<P>Anything ECM controlled with DOT legal exhaust should pass emmision testing fairly easy. <P>A traditional carb setup and HEI with mechanical advance is going to likely need really careful tuning but should be able to get passed. It's likely to take a bunch of tweeking.<P>You also want to make sure that the vapor canister is hooked up and looks right. They check the fuel system for air leaks in some states now. Part of that process is clamping the tank vent line to the canister. ((They even test gas caps in DE))<P>You want the canister hooked up anyway. Your just giving away gas if you don't. The canister is fairly easy to hook up. The large purge line goes to manifold vacuum and the control line goes to ventury vacuum. When the throttle opens far enough to pull a good vac in the top of the carb it will also open the purge valve. When the purge valve opens the vapor is sucked into the manifold thru the thick line. (The thin  control line only opens the valve.)||||reg||1
Z||000010||fotofrank||09-25-2000||05:25 PM||||I donot know for sure but, it has been said that a fuel/air guage is a big help in passing emissions with a carbed V8. The guy I spoke to in Illinois said he failed twice and didnot know what to do next. He had tuned the heck out of his system. An alternitive is TBI injection. With some carefull work it can be as good as a carb or even TPI.(so they say)<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1~ns4.html||||reg||4
